{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485, F1 0.464), the most fundamental uncertainty is whether the image modality carries any useful signal for this task. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest single-variable comparison to config_001: it holds profile setting (singleprofile) and structural simplicity (no aggregation, no fusion) constant while switching modality from RNA to image. If image accuracy is substantially higher, it justifies investing further experiments in multimodal fusion and ViT encoders; if it is comparable or lower, it suggests RNA is the primary signal and the search should focus on RNA encoder and profile/aggregation choices. This experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most consequential design axis (modality) before committing budget to more complex multimodal or multiprofile configurations."
}

